Slicks'n'Slide - native Amiga port 0.1
===================================

Download this installer package and the original shareware Slix151.zip:
https://www.slicksnslide.com/webapi/download.php?p=dos-slix&v=Slix151.zip

Unpack this LHA to disk, open its drawer and double-click Install. Select the
original ZIP when asked; leave it compressed. The self-contained helper checks
the supported publisher ZIP before extracting the two data files and 195 tracks.
It never installs the DOS executable, DOSBox, configuration or a registration key.
No host computer, external UnZip utility or PC emulator is needed to install/play.

Requirements
------------
Standalone: PAL A1200, 68020, AGA, 2 MiB Chip RAM, AmigaOS 3.x and SetPatch.
Installer 43+ is needed for the installation script; IconX launches Play from
Workbench. These are Amiga system tools, not included in this archive.
Close other applications on a 2 MiB machine. Allow about 1 MB free RAM for the
extraction helper, at least 2 MB temporary DISK space and 3 MB destination space.
Do not choose RAM: or T: as scratch on a memory-constrained Amiga.

The optional WHDLoad icon requires WHDLoad 17+ and extra Fast RAM. The slave
reserves 2 MiB Chip plus 1 MiB expansion memory and 512 KiB Kickstart space;
the host OS, WHDLoad and PRELOAD need additional memory. Tested with 2 MiB Chip
and 4 MiB Fast RAM, including PRELOAD. Standalone does not require WHDLoad.
Supply your legally obtained Kickstart 3.1 image and matching RTB in
Devs:Kickstarts (or WHDCOMMON:): kick40063.A600, kick40068.A1200 or
kick40068.A4000, each accompanied by its .RTB file. Nothing is downloaded or
redistributed by this installer. WHDLoad/RTB information: https://www.whdload.de/

Playing
-------
Double-click Play for standalone, or SlicksWHDLoad if you chose that option.
From a Shell: CD to the installed Slicks drawer, then Execute Play.
The installed data/ drawer holds the native executable, original data, tracks,
configuration, driver profiles, saved championships and optional SLICKS.REK.
Both launch methods share these files. Keep the drawer writable.

Menu controls: arrows, Enter, Escape; F1 for help. Configure drivers and controls
in the original native menus. Exit through the menu to save pending changes.
Page Up/Down in menus and help: keypad 9/3, or the two keys immediately right
of P ([ and ] on a US keyboard). Text entry and driving bindings are unchanged.
WHDLoad F10 quits immediately and cannot perform deferred game saves.
Amiga Help replaces PC Scroll Lock for shop screenshots.

Registration
------------
Support the original author by registering. Place your own valid SLICKS.REK in
the installed data/ drawer. Shareware restrictions/reminders remain without it;
valid registration enables the original registered functionality. Invalid keys
are rejected. This package contains no key or bypass. Updating the port keeps
keys and saves. Choose Keep when asked about existing data to preserve modified
tracks/records; Reinstall replaces the 195 supplied tracks and both data files.
Failed extraction does not replace installed files. If publication/copying
fails due to disk space, retain the staging drawer and rerun the installer.

Status and credits
------------------
This is a development release, not a 50 FPS guarantee. The display is PAL 50 Hz
but heavy gameplay updates still exceed 20 ms. Manual hardware-joystick testing
and exhaustive original-game compatibility are not complete.
Original game: Timo Kauppinen. Amiga port: Vesa Halttunen (Vesuri).
WHDLoad kick31/kickfs framework: WHDLoad SDK (public domain).
ZIP DEFLATE decoding: Mark Adler's puff 2.3, zlib licence; see puff-license.txt
in the installer drawer.
Installer/icon conventions follow the Vette and Rescue on Fractalus projects.
Further third-party acknowledgements are in the installer drawer's CREDITS.txt.
No game data, registration keys, ROMs, RTBs, OS tools or WHDLoad binary are shipped.
Source and detailed validation: https://github.com/Vesuri/slicks
